      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "ping",
          "label": "Start",
          "danger": "none",
          "kind": "builtin",
          "note": "Runs ping with the request fields; returns PingAck-style text plus summary. Stock writes OBJ_DEVPING_ID (PINGDiag row 0) DiagnosticsState=Requested and polls PingAck every 3 s."
        }
      ],
      "notes": "Stock mechanism: dev_ping_gch.gch, on IF_ACTION=new, does set_inst(OBJ_DEVPING_ID, \"\") with Host, Interface from the form plus fixed DiagnosticsState=Requested, NumofRepeat=4, DataBlockSize=56, Timeout=2000, then undoDBSave() (not persisted to flash). The JS then re-submits every 3 s (IF_TIME starts at 8 tries) until OBJ_DEVPING_ID PingAck is non-empty and shows PingAck verbatim in a textarea. The genuine v9 firmware (networkdiag_ping_lua.lua) also reads MinimumResponseTime, MaximumResponseTime, AverageResponseTime, SuccessCount, FailureCount, DSCP. DB backing: view IGD.PINGDIAG.CFG1 = table PINGDiag row 0 (DMs ViewName, DiagnosticsState (stored numeric, 0=idle), Interface, Host, NumberOfRepetitions, DataBlockSize, TTL, DSCP, Timeout, Interval, Stop, HaveResult); note OBJ param NumofRepeat maps to DM NumberOfRepetitions. PINGDiag rows 1-3 (CFG2-4) are other ping users (TR-069/keepalive) - do not touch. Recommended backend: builtin action that runs busybox `ping -c N -s SIZE -W secs [-I <ifname>] HOST` directly and streams output, instead of driving PINGDiag. UI-text notes moved here: [Host]: Stock accepts an IPv4 address, an IPv6 address or a host name (checkIpAddress / checkIPV6Address / checkHostName); trailing spaces trimmed, leading zeros stripped from IPv4. | [Interface]: WAN connection view name (e.g. a WANC/WCIP/WCPPP identity such as IGD.WD1.WCD1.WCIP1). Options come from the live WAN list (stock wan_query.gch / wanQueryByApp). Empty = default route. | [NumofRepeat]: Stock fixes this at 4; not editable there. | [DataBlockSize]: Stock fixes this at 56. | [Timeout]: Stock fixes this at 2000. | [DiagnosticsState]: Value strings beyond Requested are TR-098 standard names; verify on device. | [PingAck]: Raw ping output; empty while running."
    },
