      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "traceroute",
          "label": "Start",
          "danger": "none",
          "kind": "builtin",
          "note": "Runs traceroute with the request fields; stock sets OBJ_TRACERT_ID DiagnosticsState=Requested, Control=0."
        },
        {
          "id": "traceroute-stop",
          "label": "Stop",
          "danger": "none",
          "kind": "builtin",
          "note": "Stock sets OBJ_TRACERT_ID Control=1 (IF_ACTION=stop)."
        }
      ],
      "notes": "Stock mechanism: trace_route_gch.gch uses OBJ_TRACERT_ID (no DB table; runtime only). Start: IF_ACTION=start, Control=0, set_inst with Host, Interface, Timeout, MaxHopCount, Flag, Protocol, Control and DiagnosticsState=Requested (skipped if Flag already 1). Stop: IF_ACTION=stop, Control=1 (skipped if Flag 0). undoDBSave() afterwards. The JS polls every 3 s while Flag==1, up to IF_MAXTIME=500 tries, then shows \"FAIL\". Result holds a path to a text file with the traceroute output (read_file). Recommended backend: builtin action running busybox `traceroute [-I] -m HOPS -w SECS [-i <ifname>] HOST`. UI-text notes moved here: [Host]: IPv4, host name, or IPv6 when env DevIPv6Effect != 0. | [Interface]: WAN connection view name (e.g. a WANC/WCIP/WCPPP identity such as IGD.WD1.WCD1.WCIP1). Options come from the live WAN list (stock wan_query.gch / wanQueryByApp). Empty = default route. Stock list from wanQueryByApp(\"traceroute\"). | [MaxHopCount]: Stock: 1-64; empty is sent as 0 (= daemon default). | [Timeout]: Stock requires a value 1-4294967295; unit not shown by stock (TR-098 TraceRoute Timeout is ms). | [Result]: Stock: Result is a file path; the page prints read_file(Result)."
    },
